{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792960555,"nonce":"EF22TintYMudbJ0xyLJL2hVOo2Q=","message":"Local development runtime verified on the NUC (SSH alias nuc, raikage): MSB 0.7.11 installed under ~/.microsandbox/bin with ~/.local/bin/msb symlink. Doctor confirms KVM access and a ready host. No shell profile changes or system service were installed.\n\nRan two Alpine 3.23 guests, each 1 vCPU / 256 MiB, network denied and no host mounts. A file created in guest A was absent in guest B; B could not access the host SSH directory; A retained its own file. Both guests were removed and msb ls confirms no sandboxes remain.\n\nThe host filesystem has no reflink support. MSB uses private sparse copies, which is suitable for the development probe but has startup/storage costs to measure with a Haxe image. This validates the local isolation runtime, not a shipped session provider, PTY bridge, or Cloudflare integration. Logs are in bin/msb-nuc-{install,doctor,isolation,cleanup}.log.","files":null}]}